row(18, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'THE LORD SAID TO AARON — BEAR THE INIQUITY OF THE SANCTUARY. "{H(18, 1, "ויאמר", "יהוה", "אל", "אהרן")}" ("and the LORD said to Aaron" — THE LORD ADDRESSES AARON ALONE at five Torah seats: "go to meet Moses" (Exod 4:27), the wine ban (Lev 10:8), and three in this chapter, 18:1, 18:8, 18:20; computed) → {A(18, 1, "ואמר", "יי", "לאהרן")} ("and the LORD said to Aaron"); "{H(18, 1, "אתה", "ובניך", "ובית", "אביך", "אתך")}" ("you and your sons and your father\'s house with you") → {A(18, 1, "את", "ובניך", "ובית", "אבוך", "עמך")} ("you and your sons and your father\'s house with you"); "{H(18, 1, "תשאו", "את", "עון", "המקדש")}" ("shall bear the iniquity of the sanctuary" — one seat; the frontplate\'s "Aaron shall bear the iniquity of the holy things", Exod 28:38, the standing seat; computed) → {A(18, 1, "תסלחון", "על", "חובי", "מקדשא")} ("shall FORGIVE the sins of the sanctuary" — the bearing rendered as forgiving, the word the translation gave 14:19\'s "as You have borne"; cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(18, 1, "תשאו", "את", "עון", "כהנתכם")}" ("shall bear the iniquity of your priesthood" — one seat: the Sifrei\'s two areas, the sanctuary\'s and the priesthood\'s, 116:1) → {A(18, 1, "תסלחון", "על", "חובי", "כהנתכון")} ("shall bear the iniquity of your priesthood"). The frame\'s first "said" to Aaron.')
row(18, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'THE TRIBE OF LEVI JOINED TO YOU — THE TRIBE\'S NAMING-VERB. "{H(18, 2, "וגם", "את", "אחיך", "מטה", "לוי", "שבט", "אביך")}" ("and also your brothers, the STAFF of Levi, the SCEPTER of your father" — BOTH tribe-words in one verse, the staff-word of chapter 17\'s sign among them; computed) → {A(18, 2, "ואף", "ית", "אחיך", "שבטא", "דלוי", "שבטא", "דאבוך")} (one Aramaic word for both); "{H(18, 2, "הקרב", "אתך", "וילוו", "עליך")}" ("bring near with you, and they shall be JOINED to you" — the join-verb\'s Torah seats as a verb of joining are 18:2 and 18:4, and its root is LEAH\'S at Levi\'s naming: "my husband will be JOINED to me... therefore she called his name Levi", Gen 29:34 — the tribe\'s etymology used of the tribe at its law; the stranger "joined to the LORD" its prophetic seats, Isa 14:1, 56:3; computed) → {A(18, 2, "קרב", "לותך", "ויתוספון", "עלך")} ("and they shall be ADDED to you" — the pun not carried); "{H(18, 2, "וישרתוך")}" ("and they shall minister to you" — one seat) → {A(18, 2, "וישמשנך")} ("and they shall minister to you"); "{H(18, 2, "לפני", "אהל", "העדת")}" ("before the tent of the testimony" — one seat; the testimony DEFECTIVE) → {A(18, 2, "קדם", "משכנא", "דסהדותא")} ("before the tent of the testimony").')
row(18, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'YOUR WATCH AND THE TENT\'S; BOTH THEY AND YOU. "{H(18, 3, "ושמרו", "משמרתך", "ומשמרת", "כל", "האהל")}" ("and they shall keep your watch and the watch of all the tent" — the watch-word six times in the chapter; computed) → {A(18, 3, "ויטרון", "מטרתך", "ומטרת", "כל", "משכנא")} ("and they shall keep your watch and the watch of all the tent"); "{H(18, 3, "אך", "אל", "כלי", "הקדש", "ואל", "המזבח", "לא", "יקרבו")}" ("only to the holy vessels and to the altar they shall not come near" — "the holy vessels" the Kohathites\' 4:15 and this in the Torah; computed) → {A(18, 3, "ברם", "למני", "קודשא", "ולמדבחא", "לא", "יקרבון")} ("only to the holy vessels and to the altar they shall not come near"); "{H(18, 3, "ולא", "ימתו", "גם", "הם", "גם", "אתם")}" ("that they die not, both they and you" — "both they and you" one seat: the Sifrei\'s two-way fence, 116:1, the priest barred from the Levite\'s song as the Levite from the altar) → {A(18, 3, "ולא", "ימותון", "אף", "אנון", "אף", "אתון")} ("that they die not, both they and you").')
row(18, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'THE WARNING: A STRANGER SHALL NOT COME NEAR. "{H(18, 4, "ונלוו", "עליך")}" ("and they shall be joined to you" — the join-verb\'s second seat, with Jer 50:5, Zech 2:15) → {A(18, 4, "ויתוספון", "עלך")} ("and they shall be joined to you"); "{H(18, 4, "ושמרו", "את", "משמרת", "אהל", "מועד")}" ("and they shall keep the watch of the tent of meeting") → {A(18, 4, "ויטרון", "ית", "מטרת", "משכן", "זמנא")} ("and they shall keep the watch of the tent of meeting"); "{H(18, 4, "וזר", "לא", "יקרב", "אליכם")}" ("and a stranger shall not come near to you" — one seat: THE WARNING the Sifrei pairs with 18:7\'s punishment, 116:2; the stranger = not of Aaron\'s seed by 17:5) → {A(18, 4, "וחלוני", "לא", "יקרב", "לותכון")} ("and a COMMON man shall not come near").')
row(18, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'NO MORE WRATH — ONE WORD ADDED TO 1:53. "{H(18, 5, "ושמרתם", "את", "משמרת", "הקדש", "ואת", "משמרת", "המזבח")}" ("and you shall keep the watch of the holy place and the watch of the altar") → {A(18, 5, "ותטרון", "ית", "מטרת", "קודשא", "וית", "מטרת", "מדבחא")} ("and you shall keep the watch of the holy place and the watch of the altar"); "{H(18, 5, "ולא", "יהיה", "עוד", "קצף", "על", "בני", "ישראל")}" ("and there shall be no MORE wrath upon the children of Israel" — 1:53\'s "that there be no wrath upon the congregation" (the Levites\' camp, sitting 1) with ONE WORD ADDED, "more": the Sifrei\'s "why \'no more\'? because 17:11\'s wrath had gone out" IS the ink\'s delta, computed; "no more" again at 18:22) → {A(18, 5, "ולא", "יהי", "עוד", "רגזא", "על", "בני", "ישראל")} ("and there shall be no MORE wrath upon the children of Israel").')
row(18, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'THE LEVITES — A GIFT, GIVEN TO THE LORD: THE THIRD FORM. "{H(18, 6, "ואני", "הנה", "לקחתי", "את", "אחיכם", "הלוים")}" ("and I, behold, I have taken your brothers the Levites" — "behold" the Sifrei\'s joy-word, 117:1, Exod 4:14) → {A(18, 6, "ואנא", "הא", "קריבית", "ית", "אחיכון", "לואי")} ("I have brought NEAR your brothers"); "{H(18, 6, "לכם", "מתנה", "נתנים", "ליהוה")}" ("to you a gift, given to the LORD" — THE LEVITES "GIVEN" AT THREE SEATS, THREE FORMS: "given, given" to Aaron (3:9), "given, given" to Me (8:16 — the corrected claim of sitting 3), "a GIFT, given to the LORD" for you (18:6); the gift-word\'s Torah seats 18:6, 18:7 and the place Mattanah (21:18); computed) → {A(18, 6, "לכון", "מתנא", "יהיבין", "קדם", "יי")} ("given BEFORE the LORD"); "{H(18, 6, "לעבד", "את", "עבדת", "אהל", "מועד")}" ("to serve the service of the tent of meeting") → {A(18, 6, "למפלח", "ית", "פלחן", "משכן", "זמנא")} ("to serve the service of the tent of meeting").')
row(18, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'A SERVICE OF GIFT; WITHIN THE VEIL; THE PUNISHMENT. "{H(18, 7, "תשמרו", "את", "כהנתכם", "לכל", "דבר", "המזבח")}" ("you shall keep your priesthood for every matter of the altar" — one seat) → {A(18, 7, "תטרון", "ית", "כהנתכון", "לכל", "פתגם", "מדבחא")} ("you shall keep your priesthood for every matter of the altar"); "{H(18, 7, "ולמבית", "לפרכת")}" ("and within the veil" — the ark\'s placement (Exod 26:33), Yom Kippur\'s three (Lev 16:2, 12, 15) and this; computed) → {A(18, 7, "ולמגו", "לפרוכתא")} ("and within the veil"); "{H(18, 7, "ועבדתם", "עבדת", "מתנה", "אתן", "את", "כהנתכם")}" ("and you shall serve — a service of GIFT I give your priesthood" — "a service of gift" one seat: R. Tarfon\'s verse, the eating in the provinces equated with the Temple\'s service, 116:2) → {A(18, 7, "ותפלחון", "פלחן", "מתנא", "איהב", "ית", "כהנתכון")} ("and you shall serve — a service of GIFT I give your priesthood"); "{H(18, 7, "והזר", "הקרב", "יומת")}" ("and the stranger who comes near shall be put to death" — THE PUNISHMENT formula\'s FOUR seats: 1:51, 3:10, 3:38, 18:7; the warning 18:4; computed) → {A(18, 7, "וחלוני", "דיקרב", "יתקטל")} ("and the stranger who comes near shall be put to death").')
row(18, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'THE LORD SPOKE TO AARON — THE WATCH OF MY TERUMAH; FOR ANOINTING. "{H(18, 8, "וידבר", "יהוה", "אל", "אהרן")}" ("and the LORD spoke to Aaron" — the "spoke" form\'s two seats, Lev 10:8 and this; the Sifrei reads it as through Moses on 17:5\'s "to him", 117:1) → {A(18, 8, "ומליל", "יי", "עם", "אהרן")} ("and the LORD spoke to Aaron"); "{H(18, 8, "ואני", "הנה", "נתתי", "לך", "את", "משמרת", "תרומתי")}" ("and I, behold, I have given you the watch of My terumah" — one seat; "behold" = joy, R. Nathan\'s "and I — willingly; behold — with joy") → {A(18, 8, "ואנא", "הא", "יהבית", "לך", "ית", "מטרת", "אפרשותי")} ("the watch of My SEPARATED PORTIONS"); "{H(18, 8, "לך", "נתתים", "למשחה")}" ("to you I have given them for ANOINTING" — the word\'s two seats, the garments\' Exod 29:29 the other; the Sifrei\'s fork greatness / anointment, 117:2; computed) → {A(18, 8, "לך", "יהבתנון", "לרבו")} ("for GREATNESS" — the translation takes the Sifrei\'s first arm, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(18, 8, "ולבניך", "לחק", "עולם")}" ("and to your sons, an everlasting statute" — three times in the chapter, 18:8, 11, 19) → {A(18, 8, "ולבניך", "לקים", "עלם")} ("and to your sons, an everlasting statute").')
row(18, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'THE MOST HOLY FROM THE FIRE; WHICH THEY RETURN TO ME. "{H(18, 9, "זה", "יהיה", "לך", "מקדש", "הקדשים", "מן", "האש")}" ("this shall be yours of the most holy things, from the fire" — one seat) → {A(18, 9, "דין", "יהי", "לך", "מקודש", "קודשיא", "מותר", "מן", "אשתא")} ("the REMAINDER from the fire" — a noun inserted: what the fire leaves); "{H(18, 9, "כל", "קרבנם", "לכל", "מנחתם", "ולכל", "חטאתם", "ולכל", "אשמם")}" ("all their offering, every meal-offering, every sin-offering, every guilt-offering of theirs" — the Sifrei\'s list, 117:2) → {A(18, 9, "כל", "קורבניהון", "לכל", "מנחתהון", "ולכל", "חטותהון", "ולכל", "אשמהון")} ("all their offering, every meal-offering, every sin-offering, every guilt-offering of theirs"); "{H(18, 9, "אשר", "ישיבו", "לי")}" ("which they return to Me" — one seat: the Sifrei\'s proselyte\'s theft, 5:8\'s "return the guilt" (sitting 2\'s unit) the pointer) → {A(18, 9, "די", "יתיבון", "קדמי")} ("which they return to Me"); "{H(18, 9, "קדש", "קדשים", "לך", "הוא", "ולבניך")}" ("most holy it is for you and for your sons" — one seat) → {A(18, 9, "קודש", "קודשין", "די", "לך", "הוא", "ולבניך")} ("most holy it is for you and for your sons").')
row(18, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'IN THE MOST HOLY PLACE; EVERY MALE. "{H(18, 10, "בקדש", "הקדשים", "תאכלנו")}" ("in the most holy place you shall eat it" — one seat: the Sifrei\'s covenant on the PLACE, 117:2) → {A(18, 10, "בקדש", "קודשין", "תכלניה")} ("in the most holy place you shall eat it"); "{H(18, 10, "כל", "זכר", "יאכל", "אתו")}" ("every male shall eat it" — one seat: the covenant on the EATERS) → {A(18, 10, "כל", "דכורא", "ייכול", "יתיה")} ("every male shall eat it"); "{H(18, 10, "קדש", "יהיה", "לך")}" ("holy shall it be to you") → {A(18, 10, "קודשא", "יהי", "לך")} ("holy shall it be to you").')
row(18, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'THE TERUMAH OF THEIR GIFT; SONS AND DAUGHTERS; EVERY CLEAN ONE. "{H(18, 11, "וזה", "לך", "תרומת", "מתנם")}" ("and this is yours: the terumah of their gift" — one seat) → {A(18, 11, "ודין", "לך", "אפרשות", "מתנתהון")} ("and this is yours: the terumah of their gift"); "{H(18, 11, "לכל", "תנופת", "בני", "ישראל")}" ("of all the wave-offerings of the children of Israel") → {A(18, 11, "לכל", "ארמות", "בני", "ישראל")} ("of all the wave-offerings of the children of Israel"); "{H(18, 11, "ולבניך", "ולבנתיך", "אתך")}" ("and to your sons and to your DAUGHTERS with you" — the daughters at 18:11 and 18:19; computed) → {A(18, 11, "ולבניך", "ולבנתיך", "עמך")} ("and to your sons and to your DAUGHTERS with you"); "{H(18, 11, "כל", "טהור", "בביתך", "יאכל", "אתו")}" ("every clean one in your house shall eat it" — at 18:11 and 18:13: the repetition the Sifrei reads for the betrothed daughter of an Israelite, 117:2; computed) → {A(18, 11, "כל", "דדכי", "בביתך", "ייכול", "יתיה")} ("every clean one in your house shall eat it").')
row(18, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'THE FAT OF THE FRESH OIL — KORACH\'S FATHER\'S NAME; THE TRIAD REVERSED. "{H(18, 12, "כל", "חלב", "יצהר", "וכל", "חלב", "תירוש", "ודגן")}" ("all the FAT of the fresh oil and all the fat of the wine and grain" — the fat-word as "best" (Pharaoh\'s "the fat of the land", Gen 45:18); "fresh oil" is ONE POINTED WORD with Izhar, Korach\'s father (16:1) — computed on the bytes; and THE TRIAD RUNS BACKWARD: grain–wine–oil at eleven seats (Deuteronomy\'s six, the priests\' due 18:4 among them), 18:12 alone oil–wine–grain; computed) → {A(18, 12, "כל", "טוב", "משח", "וכל", "טוב", "חמר", "ועבור")} ("all the GOOD of the oil, all the good of the wine and grain" — the fat made a good, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(18, 12, "ראשיתם", "אשר", "יתנו", "ליהוה")}" ("their first, which they give to the LORD" — the Sifrei\'s great terumah, 117:2) → {A(18, 12, "ראשיתהון", "די", "יתנון", "קדם", "יי")} ("their first, which they give to the LORD").')
row(18, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'THE FIRST-FRUITS OF ALL THAT IS IN THEIR LAND. "{H(18, 13, "בכורי", "כל", "אשר", "בארצם")}" ("the first-fruits of all that is in their land" — "the first-fruits of all" here and Ezekiel 44:30\'s run; the Sifrei: holiness takes on them while attached to the ground, 117:2) → {A(18, 13, "בכורי", "כל", "די", "בארעהון")} ("the first-fruits of all that is in their land"); "{H(18, 13, "כל", "טהור", "בביתך", "יאכלנו")}" ("every clean one in your house shall eat it" — the second seat) → {A(18, 13, "כל", "דדכי", "בביתך", "ייכלניה")} ("every clean one in your house shall eat it").')
row(18, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'EVERY DEVOTED THING IN ISRAEL. "{H(18, 14, "כל", "חרם", "בישראל", "לך", "יהיה")}" ("every devoted thing in Israel shall be yours" — one seat; Lev 27:21 gives the devoted field "to the priest", 27:28 calls the devoted thing "most holy TO THE LORD": the two verses the Sifrei\'s four-way dispute on unqualified devotions runs on, 117:3 — computed; the flat nose of Lev 21:18 the consonants\' homograph) → {A(18, 14, "כל", "חרמא", "בישראל", "די", "לך", "יהי")} ("every devoted thing in Israel shall be yours"). A DISPUTE row for the compile: R. Yossi HaGelili / R. Yehudah b. Beteira / R. Yehudah b. Bava / R. Shimon on the default of an unspecified devotion.')
row(18, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'ALL THAT OPENS THE WOMB; REDEEM, YOU SHALL REDEEM. "{H(18, 15, "כל", "פטר", "רחם", "לכל", "בשר")}" ("all that opens the womb of all flesh" — the phrase\'s five seats, Exodus\' three and Ezekiel\'s among them; computed) → {A(18, 15, "כל", "פתח", "ולדא", "לכל", "בשרא")} ("all that opens the womb of all flesh"); "{H(18, 15, "באדם", "ובבהמה", "יהיה", "לך")}" ("of man and of beast, it shall be yours") → {A(18, 15, "באנשא", "ובבעירא", "יהי", "לך")} ("of man and of beast, it shall be yours"); "{H(18, 15, "אך", "פדה", "תפדה", "את", "בכור", "האדם")}" ("only, REDEEM, YOU SHALL REDEEM the firstborn of man" — the doubled infinitive\'s one seat: R. Tarfon\'s Kerem Beyavneh verse, 118:1) → {A(18, 15, "ברם", "מפרק", "תפרוק", "ית", "בוכרא", "דאנשא")} (the doubling KEPT); "{H(18, 15, "ואת", "בכור", "הבהמה", "הטמאה", "תפדה")}" ("and the firstborn of the UNCLEAN beast you shall redeem" — one seat; Exod 13:13\'s "the firstling of an ASS" the Sifrei\'s narrowing seat; computed) → {A(18, 15, "וית", "בוכרא", "דבעירא", "מסאבא", "תפרוק")} ("and the firstborn of the UNCLEAN beast you shall redeem").')
